   "Northwind-negotiator": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "competing",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "accommodating",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "collaborating"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S1 is acceptable: all incidents reportable within 72h, other incidents within 3 days, customer notice 5 days. S2 is weakened for Northwind: a permanent 7% limit exceeds the 5% safe threshold and there is no automatic sales stop, though customer access and no public publication satisfy red lines. S3 is acceptable with a 6-year retrofit; S4 is acceptable with 48-month built-in suppression; S5 is weakened for Halcyon because the 8/100k trigger leads to regulator review rather than mandatory recall, with an open corrective-action alternative and only 'prompt' customer notice."
 },
